        <h1>Job Application Tracker Project</h1>
        <h2 class="text-center mb-4">Martin Medina</h2>

        <section>
            <h2>Project Overview</h2>

            <p class="bio">
                The Job Application Tracker is a full-stack web development
                project designed to help job seekers organize their applications
                in one location instead of relying on separate websites,
                emails, documents, and notes.
            </p>

            <p class="bio">
                The project is based on the challenge of remembering application
                details, deadlines, interviews, and follow-up dates during a job
                search. Its goal is to provide a more organized way to review
                job opportunities and follow their progress.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Planned Project Features</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Record company names and job positions.</li>
                <li>Track application statuses.</li>
                <li>Store interview dates and related information.</li>
                <li>Record salary details and job requirements.</li>
                <li>Save job posting links for future reference.</li>
                <li>Add personal notes to individual applications.</li>
                <li>Organize follow-up dates and important deadlines.</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="bio">
                These are planned application capabilities. Their availability
                will depend on the features implemented in the final application.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
